⚡️ How Kyiv's Bridges Are Operating Now: Current Restrictions After the Night Attack

As a result of this morning's strike, the Podilsko-Voskresensky, Darnytskyi and Southern bridges were damaged. Current status:

▪️ Northern Bridge — private car traffic prohibited. Only public and emergency transport allowed;
▪️ Podilsko-Voskresensky Bridge — traffic from the right bank to the left bank closed following the attack. Traffic in the opposite direction remains open, but may be temporarily restricted during air alerts;
▪️ Metro Bridge — road traffic without restrictions;
▪️ Paton Bridge — open, with a reversible lane in effect:
— From 06:00 to 16:00 — toward the right bank.
— From 16:00 to 24:00 — toward the left bank.
▪️ Darnytskyi Bridge — traffic without additional restrictions, despite damage from this morning's attack;
▪️ Southern Bridge — traffic allowed only from the left bank to the right bank, at controlled intervals. Open to vehicles up to 10 tons and public transport up to 18 tons. Traffic in the opposite direction is prohibited.
